From 38c3cea06b2d5fcdcb8c185b036515f6fee49b26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 02:56:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/41] Reconstruct the per-CPU advanced TCP timer subsystem

Recover all 28 functions of bsd/netinet/tcp_timer_advanced.c from the
release-kernel disassembly, each annotated with its reference
file:line, plus the inline API in tcp_timer_advanced.h:

- the te_node/te_next/te_free/te_tp/te_inp/te_expires layout and the
  four inline accessors (schedule, cancel, isactive, get_value)
- RB tree management (RB_GENERATE over te_expires with a pointer
  tiebreak) with tree_remove/calculate_softexpires/entry alloc and
  freelist handling
- tcp_timer_advanced_add/remove/cleanup with the inlined
  socket_lock_assert_owned and the TF_TIMER_ENTRY_USECOUNT socket
  usecount handoff
- the per-CPU thread_call: invoke_handler, process_cpu_timer, the
  interface-probe snapshot/execute pair, reschedule_cpu and init.

tcp_var.h gains t_timer_entries[TCPT_NTIMERS] at tcpcb offset 0x58
(the field that shifts t_inpcb to 0xa8) and the two reused t_flags
bits, TF_TIMER_ADVANCED (0x02000000) and TF_TIMER_ENTRY_USECOUNT
(0x80000000).  tcp_offset_from_latest_tx loses its static linkage so
the header inline can call it, matching its DWARF inline location in
tcp_timer.c.

Remaining explicit stubs: 259.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
